---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const videoId = '4AEO1smpvzs';
---

<Layout
  title="Mike Trounce — Startup Consultant for Early-Stage Founders"
  description="I work with early-stage founders on fundraising and on making the story of your company something you can hand to anyone and trust it's current."
>
  <div id="top" class="hero">
    <div class="video-frame" id="video-frame" data-video-id={videoId}>
      <img
        class="video-thumb"
        src={`https://img.youtube.com/vi/${videoId}/maxresdefault.jpg`}
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
        onerror={`this.onerror=null; this.src='https://img.youtube.com/vi/${videoId}/hqdefault.jpg';`}
      />
      <button class="play-btn" id="play-btn" aria-label="Play video">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"></path></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <p class="video-caption">Click to play</p>
  </div>

  <div class="bio">
    <p>
      I&rsquo;m Mike. I work with early-stage founders on the stuff that&rsquo;s hard to do
      alone &mdash; fundraising, telling your story clearly, and getting your company organized
      enough that other people can actually understand it. Here&rsquo;s one recent example.
    </p>
    <div class="signature">Mike</div>
  </div>

  <main class="wrap">
    <section id="project">
      <span class="eyebrow">A recent project</span>
      <h2>A document that doesn&rsquo;t go stale</h2>
      <p>
        A founder I&rsquo;ve been working with is raising money right now. Like most founders at
        that stage, the real story of the company &mdash; the traction, the team, the numbers,
        the plan &mdash; lived in scattered docs and their own head, and the pitch hadn&rsquo;t
        caught up with where the company actually was.
      </p>
      <p>
        Over a handful of working sessions, we went through everything: the product, the
        customers, the financials, the people. What came out of it is a document I call the <strong>Company Memo</strong> &mdash; a
        single, always-current document they can hand to a new investor or a candidate instead of
        re-explaining everything from scratch.
      </p>
      <p>
        The part that makes it worth doing: nothing goes in until it&rsquo;s actually checked. An
        optimistic claim in conversation &mdash; &ldquo;we&rsquo;ve basically got that customer
        signed&rdquo; &mdash; gets verified and, more often than not, softened into something more
        precise before it&rsquo;s written down. And when plans change between sessions, which they
        do, the Memo tracks the change instead of quietly pretending the old version never
        existed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer id="contact">
      <span class="eyebrow">Get in touch</span>
      <h2 style="margin-bottom:14px;">Got something worth building?</h2>
      <p class="contact-line">Send me a note &mdash; I read everything myself.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:16px;"><a class="contact-email" href="mailto:trounceflow@gmail.com">trounceflow@gmail.com</a></p>
      <p class="foot-note">Mike &middot; Startup consultant for early-stage founders</p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  const frame = document.getElementById('video-frame');
  const playBtn = document.getElementById('play-btn');
  const caption = document.querySelector('.video-caption');
  if (frame && playBtn) {
    playBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const id = frame.getAttribute('data-video-id');
      const iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
      iframe.src = `https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${id}?autoplay=1&rel=0&modestbranding=1&iv_load_policy=3`;
      iframe.title = 'Video';
      iframe.allow = 'autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen';
      iframe.allowFullscreen = true;
      frame.innerHTML = '';
      frame.appendChild(iframe);
      caption?.remove();
    });
  }
</script>
